time-hourglass is a fork of hourglass that renamed its Haskell modules but kept
the C symbol prefix, so both packages export hourglass_clock_calendar. sauron's
plan contains both -- time-hourglass via crypton-asn1-types, and hourglass via
authenticate-oauth -> RSA -> crypto-pubkey-types -> asn1-types (which is stuck
on hourglass; 0.3.4 is the newest asn1-types and nothing newer exists).

A dynamic GHC never notices, but the static-by-default GHC a musl static build
needs loads real object files for TemplateHaskell splices, and its runtime
linker rejects the duplicate:

  GHC runtime linker: fatal error: I found a duplicate definition for symbol
     hourglass_clock_calendar

Renaming time-hourglass's copy is the smallest fix; it is one C definition and
one foreign import. Note both files use CRLF, so this patch does too.

--- a/cbits/unix.c
+++ b/cbits/unix.c
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
  * we ignore errors as it's very very unlikely considering the hardcoded ID
  * and the fact that haskell should call this code.
  */
-void hourglass_clock_calendar(struct timespec *timespec)
+void time_hourglass_clock_calendar(struct timespec *timespec)
 {
 #if defined __MACH__ && !defined __GNU__
 	clock_serv_t cclock;
--- a/src/unix/Time/Internal.hs
+++ b/src/unix/Time/Internal.hs
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@
   toElapsed :: CTime -> Elapsed
   toElapsed (CTime sec) = Elapsed $ Seconds (fromIntegral sec)
 
-foreign import ccall unsafe "hourglass_clock_calendar"
+foreign import ccall unsafe "time_hourglass_clock_calendar"
   c_clock_get :: Ptr CLong -> IO ()
 
 foreign import ccall unsafe "gmtime_r"
